IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`

-- coa26-ch3a.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 42, Chapter 3 (Auditors General), ss 1226 to 1231: eligibility of an Auditor General,
-- audit work on an Auditor General's behalf, the appointment of the Independent Supervisor, supervision of Auditors General,
-- their duties under the supervision arrangements, and the Independent Supervisor's annual report.
-- Lines 17386-17456 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. (ss 1232-1238 are in coa26-ch3b.l4.)
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa26-ch1.l4 (MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, each such branch
-- with a FALSE-kind comment; NOTHING otherwise, each branch with a NOTHING-kind comment). A duty is asked as "has the person done what
-- the subsection requires": JUST TRUE when done; JUST FALSE when not done (a bare "must": decided case by case, see the fork register);
-- JUST FALSE too when the "if" or "where" that starts the duty is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b) and the keel's reading (a)).

§§ `Chapter 3 -- Auditors General`

§§§ `Eligibility for appointment (s 1226)`

-- src:17389 | (1) In this Part “Auditor General” means—
-- src:17390 | (a) the Comptroller and Auditor General,
-- src:17391 | (b) the Auditor General for Scotland,
-- src:17392 | (c) the Auditor General for Wales, or
-- src:17393 | (d) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1226(1) "Auditor General" (src:17389-17393)
GIVEN `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Auditor General for Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Auditor General for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1226(1) the person is an Auditor General` MEANS
    IF     `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General`
        OR `the person is the Auditor General for Scotland`
        OR `the person is the Auditor General for Wales`
        OR `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “Auditor General” means—"

-- src:17394 | (2) An Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor.
-- src:17395 | (3) Subsection (2) is subject to any suspension notice having effect under section 1234 (notices suspending eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor).
@ref s 1226(2) An Auditor General is eligible, subject to s 1234 (src:17394-17395)
GIVEN `the person is an Auditor General` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a suspension notice having effect under section 1234 suspends the Auditor General's eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1226(2) the Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the person is an Auditor General`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor": the subsection speaks only of an Auditor General
        IF `a suspension notice having effect under section 1234 suspends the Auditor General's eligibility` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(3) Subsection (2) is subject to any suspension notice having effect under section 1234"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§§ `Conduct of audits (s 1227)`

-- src:17398 | An Auditor General must secure that each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of that Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2.
@ref s 1227 Individuals responsible for audit work on behalf of Auditors General (src:17398)
GIVEN `the individual is responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1212(1) the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1227 the Auditor General has secured that the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` MEANS
    IF NOT `the individual is responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the Auditor General`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of that Auditor General"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1212(1) the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An Auditor General must secure that each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of that Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2." (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual is eligible by virtue of Chapter 2 is the answer of section 1212 and Schedule 10

§§§ `The Independent Supervisor (s 1228)`

-- src:17401 | (1) The Secretary of State must appoint a body (“the Independent Supervisor”) to discharge the function mentioned in section 1229(1) (“the supervision function”).
@ref s 1228(1) The Secretary of State must appoint a body (src:17401)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has appointed a body (“the Independent Supervisor”) to discharge the function mentioned in section 1229(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1228(1) the Secretary of State has appointed the Independent Supervisor` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has appointed a body (“the Independent Supervisor”) to discharge the function mentioned in section 1229(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must appoint a body (“the Independent Supervisor”) to discharge the function mentioned in section 1229(1)" (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17402 | (2) An appointment under this section must be made by order.
@ref s 1228(2) The appointment is by order (src:17402)
GIVEN `the appointment is made by order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1228(2) the appointment is made in the required form` MEANS
    IF `the appointment is made by order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appointment under this section must be made by order."

-- src:17403 | (3) The order has the effect of making the body appointed under subsection (1) designated under section 5 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (c. 36) (further powers to designate public authorities).
@ref s 1228(3) Designation under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (src:17403)
GIVEN `the order is an order appointing a body under section 1228(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1228(3) the body appointed is designated under section 5 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order appointing a body under section 1228(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order has the effect of making the body appointed under subsection (1) designated"

-- src:17407 | (5) The conditions are—
-- src:17408 | (a) that the supervision function will be exercised effectively, and
-- src:17409 | (b) where the order is to contain any requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (6), that that function will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions.
@ref s 1228(5) The conditions (src:17407-17409)
GIVEN `the supervision function will be exercised effectively` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order contains requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1228(5) the conditions in subsection (5) are met` MEANS
    IF     `the supervision function will be exercised effectively`
       AND ((NOT `the order contains requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (6)`) OR `the function will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are— (a) that the supervision function will be exercised effectively, and (b) where the order is to contain any requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (6), that that function will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions."

-- src:17404 | (4) A body may be appointed under this section only if it is a body corporate or an unincorporated association which appears to the Secretary of State—
-- src:17405 | (a) to be willing and able to discharge the supervision function, and
-- src:17406 | (b) to have arrangements in place relating to the discharge of that function which are such as to be likely to ensure that the conditions in subsection (5) are met.
@ref s 1228(4) Who may be appointed (src:17404-17406)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate or an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is willing and able to discharge the supervision function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body has arrangements in place relating to the discharge of that function which are such as to be likely to ensure that the conditions in subsection (5) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1228(4) the conditions for appointing the body are met` MEANS
    IF     `the body is a body corporate or an unincorporated association`
       AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is willing and able to discharge the supervision function`
       AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body has arrangements in place relating to the discharge of that function which are such as to be likely to ensure that the conditions in subsection (5) are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A body may be appointed under this section only if it is a body corporate or an unincorporated association which appears to the Secretary of State— (a) to be willing and able to discharge the supervision function, and (b) to have arrangements in place"

-- src:17410 | (6) An order under this section may contain such requirements or other provisions relating to the exercise of the supervision function by the Independent Supervisor as appear to the Secretary of State to be appropriate.
@ref s 1228(6) What the order may contain (src:17410)
GIVEN `the requirement or provision relates to the exercise of the supervision function by the Independent Supervisor and appears to the Secretary of State to be appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1228(6) the order may contain the requirement or provision` MEANS
    IF `the requirement or provision relates to the exercise of the supervision function by the Independent Supervisor and appears to the Secretary of State to be appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such requirements or other provisions relating to the exercise of the supervision function by the Independent Supervisor as appear to the Secretary of State to be appropriate"

-- s 1228(7) (an order under this section is subject to negative resolution procedure) is machinery (coverage: inert, reason 2).

§§§ `Supervision of Auditors General (s 1229)`

-- src:17414 | (1) The Independent Supervisor must supervise the performance by each Auditor General of his functions as a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1229(1) The Independent Supervisor must supervise each Auditor General (src:17414)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor supervises the performance by each Auditor General of his functions as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(1) the Independent Supervisor has complied with the duty to supervise the Auditors General` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor supervises the performance by each Auditor General of his functions as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must supervise the performance by each Auditor General of his functions as a statutory auditor." (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17415 | (2) The Independent Supervisor must discharge that duty by—
-- src:17416 | (a) establishing supervision arrangements itself, or
-- src:17417 | (b) entering into supervision arrangements with one or more recognised supervisory bodies.
@ref s 1229(2) How the duty is discharged (src:17415-17417)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor establishes supervision arrangements itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor enters into supervision arrangements with one or more recognised supervisory bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(2) the Independent Supervisor has discharged the duty in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor establishes supervision arrangements itself` OR `the Independent Supervisor enters into supervision arrangements with one or more recognised supervisory bodies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must discharge that duty by— (a) establishing supervision arrangements itself, or (b) entering into supervision arrangements with one or more recognised supervisory bodies."

-- src:17418 | (2A) If the Independent Supervisor enters into supervision arrangements with one or more bodies, it must oversee the effective operation of those supervision arrangements.
@ref s 1229(2A) Overseeing arrangements entered into with bodies (src:17418)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor enters into supervision arrangements with one or more bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor oversees the effective operation of those supervision arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(2A) the Independent Supervisor has complied with the duty to oversee the arrangements` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Independent Supervisor enters into supervision arrangements with one or more bodies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Independent Supervisor enters into supervision arrangements with one or more bodies" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)
    ELSE IF `the Independent Supervisor oversees the effective operation of those supervision arrangements`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must oversee the effective operation of those supervision arrangements"

-- src:17419 | (3) For this purpose “supervision arrangements” are arrangements established by the Independent Supervisor or entered into by the Independent Supervisor with a body, for the purposes of this section, in accordance with which the Independent Supervisor or the body does . . . the following—
-- src:17420 | (a) determines standards relating to professional integrity and independence which must be applied by an Auditor General in statutory audit work;
-- src:17421 | (b) determines technical standards which must be applied by an Auditor General in statutory audit work and the manner in which those standards are to be applied in practice;
-- src:17422 | (c) monitors the performance of statutory audits carried out by an Auditor General;
-- src:17423 | (d) investigates any matter arising from the performance by an Auditor General of a statutory audit;
-- src:17424 | (e) holds disciplinary hearings in respect of an Auditor General which appear to be desirable following the conclusion of such investigations;
-- src:17425 | (f) decides whether (and, if so, what) disciplinary action should be taken against an Auditor General to whom such a hearing related.
@ref s 1229(3) "supervision arrangements" (src:17419-17425)
GIVEN `the arrangements are established by the Independent Supervisor, or entered into by the Independent Supervisor with a body, for the purposes of section 1229` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body determines standards relating to professional integrity and independence which must be applied by an Auditor General in statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body determines technical standards which must be applied by an Auditor General in statutory audit work and the manner in which those standards are to be applied in practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body monitors the performance of statutory audits carried out by an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body investigates any matter arising from the performance by an Auditor General of a statutory audit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body holds disciplinary hearings in respect of an Auditor General which appear to be desirable following the conclusion of such investigations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body decides whether (and, if so, what) disciplinary action should be taken against an Auditor General to whom such a hearing related` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(3) the arrangements are supervision arrangements` MEANS
    -- the six functions (a) to (f) are listed one after the other with no "or": all six are read as required (see the fork register)
    IF     `the arrangements are established by the Independent Supervisor, or entered into by the Independent Supervisor with a body, for the purposes of section 1229`
       AND `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body determines standards relating to professional integrity and independence which must be applied by an Auditor General in statutory audit work`
       AND `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body determines technical standards which must be applied by an Auditor General in statutory audit work and the manner in which those standards are to be applied in practice`
       AND `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body monitors the performance of statutory audits carried out by an Auditor General`
       AND `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body investigates any matter arising from the performance by an Auditor General of a statutory audit`
       AND `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body holds disciplinary hearings in respect of an Auditor General which appear to be desirable following the conclusion of such investigations`
       AND `under the arrangements the Independent Supervisor or the body decides whether (and, if so, what) disciplinary action should be taken against an Auditor General to whom such a hearing related`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For this purpose “supervision arrangements” are arrangements established by the Independent Supervisor or entered into by the Independent Supervisor with a body, for the purposes of this section, in accordance with which the Independent Supervisor or the body does ... the following—"

-- src:17426 | (3A) The requirements of paragraphs 9 to 10C and 12 to 16 of Schedule 10 (requirements for recognition of a supervisory body) apply in relation to supervision arrangements as they apply in relation to the rules, practices and arrangements of supervisory bodies.
@ref s 1229(3A) Schedule 10 requirements apply to the arrangements (src:17426)
GIVEN `the requirement is a requirement of paragraphs 9 to 10C or 12 to 16 of Schedule 10 (requirements for recognition of a supervisory body)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(3A) the requirement applies in relation to the supervision arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is a requirement of paragraphs 9 to 10C or 12 to 16 of Schedule 10 (requirements for recognition of a supervisory body)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The requirements of paragraphs 9 to 10C and 12 to 16 of Schedule 10 ... apply in relation to supervision arrangements"

-- src:17427 | (4) The Independent Supervisor may enter into supervision arrangements with a body despite any relationship that may exist between the Independent Supervisor and that body.
@ref s 1229(4) Arrangements despite a relationship (src:17427)
GIVEN `a relationship exists between the Independent Supervisor and the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(4) the Independent Supervisor may enter into supervision arrangements with the body` MEANS
    IF `a relationship exists between the Independent Supervisor and the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "despite any relationship that may exist": the subsection says only that a relationship is no bar; the permission itself is in subsection (2)(b)

-- src:17428 | (5) The Independent Supervisor must notify each Auditor General in writing of any supervision arrangements that it establishes or enters into under this section.
@ref s 1229(5) Notice of the arrangements to each Auditor General (src:17428)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor establishes or enters into supervision arrangements under section 1229` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor notifies each Auditor General in writing of the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(5) the Independent Supervisor has complied with the duty to notify each Auditor General` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Independent Supervisor establishes or enters into supervision arrangements under section 1229`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of any supervision arrangements that it establishes or enters into under this section" (no arrangements, no duty: decided case by case, see the fork register)
    ELSE IF `the Independent Supervisor notifies each Auditor General in writing of the arrangements`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must notify each Auditor General in writing"

-- src:17429 | (5A) The Independent Supervisor must, at least once in every calendar year, deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of any inspections conducted for the purposes of subsection (3)(c).
@ref s 1229(5A) A summary of inspection results every calendar year (src:17429)
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the dates on which the Independent Supervisor delivered to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections conducted for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(5A) the Independent Supervisor delivered the summary in the calendar year` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN d YIELD DATE_YEAR d EQUALS `the calendar year`) `the dates on which the Independent Supervisor delivered to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections conducted for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must, at least once in every calendar year, deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of any inspections" (a period fixed in the text's own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:17430 | (6) Supervision arrangements within subsection (3)(f) may, in particular, provide for the payment by an Auditor General of a fine to any personor, in the case of the Auditor General for Wales, for payment by the Wales Audit Office of such a fine.
@ref s 1229(6) A fine under the arrangements (src:17430)
GIVEN `the arrangements are within subsection (3)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payer is the Auditor General or, in the case of the Auditor General for Wales, the Wales Audit Office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(6) the arrangements may provide for payment of a fine to any person` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements are within subsection (3)(f)` AND `the payer is the Auditor General or, in the case of the Auditor General for Wales, the Wales Audit Office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Supervision arrangements within subsection (3)(f) may, in particular, provide for the payment by an Auditor General of a fine to any person" (the rendering of the sentence runs two versions together: see the findings in NOTES.md)

-- src:17431 | (7) Any fine received by the Independent Supervisor under supervision arrangements is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 1229(7) Fines are paid into the Consolidated Fund (src:17431)
GIVEN `the fine is received by the Independent Supervisor under supervision arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1229(7) the fine is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `the fine is received by the Independent Supervisor under supervision arrangements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any fine received by the Independent Supervisor under supervision arrangements"

§§§ `Duties of Auditors General (s 1230)`

-- src:17433 | (1) Each Auditor General must—
-- src:17434 | (a) comply with any standards of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b) of section 1229 determined under the supervision arrangements,
-- src:17435 | (b) take such steps as may be reasonably required of that Auditor General to enable his performance of statutory audits to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the supervision arrangements, and
-- src:17436 | (c) comply with any decision of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(f) of that section made under the supervision arrangements.
@ref s 1230(1) Duties in relation to the supervision arrangements (src:17433-17436)
GIVEN `the Auditor General complies with any standards of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b) of section 1229 determined under the supervision arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Auditor General takes such steps as may be reasonably required of him to enable his performance of statutory audits to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the supervision arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Auditor General complies with any decision of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(f) of section 1229 made under the supervision arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1230(1) the Auditor General has complied with the duties in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF     `the Auditor General complies with any standards of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b) of section 1229 determined under the supervision arrangements`
       AND `the Auditor General takes such steps as may be reasonably required of him to enable his performance of statutory audits to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the supervision arrangements`
       AND `the Auditor General complies with any decision of the kind mentioned in subsection (3)(f) of section 1229 made under the supervision arrangements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each Auditor General must— (a) comply with any standards ..., (b) take such steps ..., and (c) comply with any decision" (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

DECLARE `s 1230(2) who the Auditor General must pay` IS ONE OF
    `s 1230(2)(a) the Independent Supervisor`
    `s 1230(2)(b) the body with which the Independent Supervisor has entered into supervision arrangements`
    `s 1230(2) nobody under this subsection`

-- src:17437 | (2) Each Auditor General must—
-- src:17438 | (a) if the Independent Supervisor has established supervision arrangements, pay to the Independent Supervisor;
-- src:17439 | (b) if the Independent Supervisor has entered into supervision arrangements with a body, pay to that body,
-- src:17440 | such proportion of the costs incurred by the Independent Supervisor or body for the purposes of the arrangements as the Independent Supervisor may notify to him in writing.
@ref s 1230(2) Paying a proportion of the costs (src:17437-17440)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor has established supervision arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor has entered into supervision arrangements with a body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1230(2) who the Auditor General must pay`
`s 1230(2) who the Auditor General must pay the proportion of the costs to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Independent Supervisor has established supervision arrangements` THEN `s 1230(2)(a) the Independent Supervisor`
        IF `the Independent Supervisor has entered into supervision arrangements with a body` THEN `s 1230(2)(b) the body with which the Independent Supervisor has entered into supervision arrangements`
        OTHERWISE `s 1230(2) nobody under this subsection`

-- src:17437 | (2) Each Auditor General must—
-- src:17438 | (a) if the Independent Supervisor has established supervision arrangements, pay to the Independent Supervisor;
-- src:17439 | (b) if the Independent Supervisor has entered into supervision arrangements with a body, pay to that body,
-- src:17440 | such proportion of the costs incurred by the Independent Supervisor or body for the purposes of the arrangements as the Independent Supervisor may notify to him in writing.
@ref s 1230(2) The amount payable (src:17437-17440)
GIVEN `the costs incurred by the Independent Supervisor or the body for the purposes of the arrangements, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of those costs the Independent Supervisor has notified to the Auditor General in writing, as a fraction` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1230(2) the amount the Auditor General must pay, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proportion of those costs the Independent Supervisor has notified to the Auditor General in writing, as a fraction`
    WHEN JUST fraction THEN JUST (`the costs incurred by the Independent Supervisor or the body for the purposes of the arrangements, in pounds` TIMES fraction)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the proportion is "such proportion ... as the Independent Supervisor may notify to him in writing"; until it is notified there is no figure

DECLARE `s 1230(3) whose expenditure it is regarded as` IS ONE OF
    `s 1230(3)(b) expenditure of the Northern Ireland Audit Office for the purposes of Article 6(1) of the Audit (Northern Ireland) Order 1987`
    `s 1230(3)(c) expenditure of the Wales Audit Office for the purposes of section 20 of the Public Audit (Wales) Act 2013`
    `s 1230(3) not covered by this subsection`

-- src:17441 | (3) Expenditure under subsection (2) is—
-- src:17442 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:17443 | (b) in the case of expenditure of the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland, to be regarded as expenditure of the Northern Ireland Audit Office for the purposes of Article 6(1) of the Audit (Northern Ireland) Order 1987 (S.I. 1987/460 (N.I. 5)).
-- src:17444 | (c) in the case of expenditure of the Auditor General for Wales, to be regarded as expenditure of the Wales Audit Office for the purposes of section 20 of the Public Audit (Wales) Act 2013.
@ref s 1230(3) Expenditure under subsection (2) (src:17441-17444)
GIVEN `the expenditure is that of the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenditure is that of the Auditor General for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1230(3) whose expenditure it is regarded as`
`s 1230(3) the expenditure is regarded as` MEANS
    -- paragraph (a) is blank in this text (coverage: repealed or blank)
    BRANCH
        IF `the expenditure is that of the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland` THEN `s 1230(3)(b) expenditure of the Northern Ireland Audit Office for the purposes of Article 6(1) of the Audit (Northern Ireland) Order 1987`
        IF `the expenditure is that of the Auditor General for Wales` THEN `s 1230(3)(c) expenditure of the Wales Audit Office for the purposes of section 20 of the Public Audit (Wales) Act 2013`
        OTHERWISE `s 1230(3) not covered by this subsection` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) is blank here and no other Auditor General is named

-- src:17445 | (4) In this section “the supervision arrangements” means the arrangements established or entered into under section 1229.
@ref s 1230(4) "the supervision arrangements" (src:17445)
GIVEN `the arrangements are the arrangements established or entered into under section 1229` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1230(4) the arrangements are the supervision arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements are the arrangements established or entered into under section 1229`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “the supervision arrangements” means the arrangements established or entered into under section 1229."

§§§ `Reporting requirement (s 1231)`

-- src:17448 | (1) The Independent Supervisor must, at least once in each calendar year, prepare a report on the discharge of its functions.
@ref s 1231(1) An annual report (src:17448)
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the dates on which the Independent Supervisor prepared a report on the discharge of its functions` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1231(1) the Independent Supervisor prepared a report in the calendar year` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN d YIELD DATE_YEAR d EQUALS `the calendar year`) `the dates on which the Independent Supervisor prepared a report on the discharge of its functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must, at least once in each calendar year, prepare a report on the discharge of its functions." (a period fixed in the text's own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:17449 | (2) The Independent Supervisor must give a copy of each report prepared under subsection (1) to—
-- src:17450 | (a) the Secretary of State;
-- src:17451 | (b) the First Minister in Scotland;
-- src:17452 | (c) the First Minister and the deputy First Minister in Northern Ireland;
-- src:17453 | (d) The First Minister for Wales.
@ref s 1231(2) Copies of the report (src:17449-17453)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the First Minister in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the First Minister and the deputy First Minister in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the First Minister for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1231(2) the Independent Supervisor has given a copy of the report to each person named` MEANS
    IF     `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the Secretary of State`
       AND `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the First Minister in Scotland`
       AND `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the First Minister and the deputy First Minister in Northern Ireland`
       AND `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the report to the First Minister for Wales`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must give a copy of each report prepared under subsection (1) to— (a) the Secretary of State; (b) the First Minister in Scotland; (c) ... (d) The First Minister for Wales." (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17454 | (3) The Secretary of State must lay before each House of Parliament a copy of each report received by him under subsection (2)(a).
@ref s 1231(3) Laying before Parliament (src:17454)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State received a report under subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State laid a copy before each House of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1231(3) the Secretary of State has laid a copy of the report before each House of Parliament` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State received a report under subsection (2)(a)` AND `the Secretary of State laid a copy before each House of Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must lay before each House of Parliament a copy of each report received by him under subsection (2)(a)." (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17455 | (3A) The First Minister for Wales must lay before the National Assembly for Wales a copy of each report received by him under subsection (2)(d).
@ref s 1231(3A) Laying before the National Assembly for Wales (src:17455)
GIVEN `the First Minister for Wales received a report under subsection (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Minister for Wales laid a copy before the National Assembly for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1231(3A) the First Minister for Wales has laid a copy of the report before the National Assembly for Wales` MEANS
    IF `the First Minister for Wales received a report under subsection (2)(d)` AND `the First Minister for Wales laid a copy before the National Assembly for Wales`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The First Minister for Wales must lay before the National Assembly for Wales a copy of each report received by him under subsection (2)(d)." (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17456 | (4) In relation to a calendar year during which an appointment of a body as the Independent Supervisor is made or revoked by an order under section 1228, this section applies with such modifications as may be specified in the order.
@ref s 1231(4) The year of an appointment or revocation (src:17456)
GIVEN `an appointment of a body as the Independent Supervisor is made or revoked by an order under section 1228 during the calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1231(4) the section applies with the modifications specified in the order` MEANS
    IF `an appointment of a body as the Independent Supervisor is made or revoked by an order under section 1228 during the calendar year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a calendar year during which an appointment of a body as the Independent Supervisor is made or revoked by an order under section 1228"
